    "result_text": "Done. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe structured address form is now accepted alongside the flat `address`, and everything downstream sees a normalized, composed `address`. Six files, each change kept small and local:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added optional `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` to `OwnerFields` (so they appear in both the request DTO and the `Owner` response DTO), and dropped `address` from the `required` list so a structured-only owner passes bean validation while remaining backward-compatible.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 two nullable `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns with plain getters/setters. MapStruct maps them by name, so no mapper edit was needed.\n\n3. **`NormalizeAddress.java`** \u2014 extracted a small `normalize(...)` helper and made `service` prefer the structured lines: when `addressLine1` is non-blank it normalizes both lines and sets `address` to the composed string (`line1`, plus `\" \" + line2` only when `line2` is present); otherwise it falls back to normalizing the flat `address`. Because it writes the composed value back into `address`, every later consumer (household check, `ApplyOwner`, etc.) transparently uses the structured value.\n\n4. **`ValidateOwnerFields.java`** \u2014 the address requirement is now \"non-blank `addressLine1` **or** non-blank `address`\", via a tiny `isBlank` helper; city/name/telephone requirements unchanged.\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql` + `data.sql`** \u2014 added the two columns (this is the test profile, `ddl-auto=none`) and padded the 10 positional seed inserts with the matching `NULL`s.\n\nThe h2 dev profile picks up the new columns automatically (`ddl-auto=update`). I left mysql/postgres schemas alone \u2014 they already omit `postcode`/`birth_date` and are out of sync with the entity independently of this change, so they aren't test-exercised.\n\nHousehold hash, postcode validation, and locality already key on the top-level `postcode`/`city` fields (shared by both address forms), so they needed no change to satisfy the \"structured when present, falling back to flat\" requirement.",
